  "body": "XML has a separate empty-element-tag production for markup such as `<video src=\"movie.webm\"/>` and `<script src=\"example.js\"/>`. The XML parsing rules currently refer to distinct start and end tags when describing children-parsed steps or script preparation.\n\nSpecify when those steps run for an empty-element tag. This also gives a parser-created media element an explicit point to clear its blocked-on-parser flag.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13265/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 9:37 AM UTC (58e1f06)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13265/0793d3d...58e1f06/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 9:37 AM UTC (58e1f06)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13265/xhtml.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 9:37 AM UTC (58e1f06)\">/xhtml.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13265/0793d3d...58e1f06/xhtml.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 16, 2026, 9:37 AM UTC (58e1f06)\">diff</a> )",
